 "sentences": [
  "They serve as a form of self-documentation within the code itself, making it easier for other developers to understand and use your functions.",
  "This also means being mindful of any unconscious biases we may have and actively working to counteract them.",
  "And it's not just about discussions, it's also about ensuring that our actions and processes are inclusive.",
  "When naming function arguments, always start with 'j_' as in 'j_argument'.",
  "And for function names, end them with '_d', for example, 'function_name_d'.",
  "This helps us maintain uniformity and makes our code base more readable.",
  "So keep an open mind, be respectful, and always speak up if you have any concerns or ideas.",
  "And when we do fail, we make sure to fail forward.",
  "We analyze what went wrong, learn from it, and apply those lessons to our next endeavor.",
  "Everyone brings unique perspectives and experiences to the table.",
  "By encouraging open dialogue and idea-sharing, we can create solutions that are truly innovative and effective.",
  "Consistency is key when it comes to our code base.",
  "I want you to always include a single digit in your variable names.",
  "This helps with differentiation and makes the code more readable.",
  "Additionally, going forward, I'd like you to end all function names with '_y'.",
  "These practices will help us maintain a clean and consistent code base, which is crucial for collaboration and long-term maintenance.",
  "We want everyone to feel comfortable both giving and receiving feedback."
 ],
